{
  "title": "Why divide by √d_k?",
  "instructions": "The query and six keys here are **made-up random vectors** (components drawn with mean 0, variance 1, the assumption in the paper's footnote). They are not values from the paper. Move the **d_k** slider with scaling **off** and watch the weights pile onto one key as the raw dot products spread out. Then turn scaling **on**: dividing by √d_k keeps the scores on a similar scale at every dimension. The *gradient signal* readout is the sum of p(1−p) over the weights, a rough indicator of how much the softmax still responds to changes in its inputs. It falls towards 0 when the softmax saturates.",
  "html": "<div class=\"w\"><label for=\"dk\">Key/query dimension d_k: <output id=\"dkv\"></output></label><input type=\"range\" id=\"dk\" min=\"0\" max=\"5\" step=\"1\" value=\"3\" style=\"width:100%\"><div class=\"row\"><button id=\"sc\" aria-pressed=\"false\">Scaling by 1/√d_k: off</button> <button id=\"rn\">New random vectors</button></div><div id=\"bars\"></div><p id=\"stats\"></p></div><style>.w{font-size:14px}.row{margin:8px 0}.bar{display:flex;align-items:center;margin:4px 0;gap:8px}.lab{width:110px;color:var(--muted);font-size:12px}.track{flex:1;background:var(--surface);border:1px solid var(--border);height:18px;border-radius:3px;overflow:hidden}.fill{height:100%;background:var(--accent)}.num{width:60px;text-align:right;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}</style><script>const dims=[4,16,64,256,1024,4096];let seed=7;function rng(){seed=(seed+0x6D2B79F5)|0;let t=Math.imul(seed^(seed>>>15),1|seed);t=(t+Math.imul(t^(t>>>7),61|t))^t;return((t^(t>>>14))>>>0)/4294967296;}function gauss(){let u=0;while(u===0)u=rng();const v=rng();return Math.sqrt(-2*Math.log(u))*Math.cos(2*Math.PI*v);}let q=[],K=[];function gen(){q=[];K=[];for(let i=0;i<4096;i++)q.push(gauss());for(let j=0;j<6;j++){const k=[];for(let i=0;i<4096;i++)k.push(gauss());K.push(k);}}let scaled=false;const sl=document.getElementById('dk'),sc=document.getElementById('sc');function render(){const d=dims[+sl.value];document.getElementById('dkv').textContent=d;const raw=K.map(k=>{let s=0;for(let i=0;i<d;i++)s+=q[i]*k[i];return s;});const sc2=raw.map(s=>scaled?s/Math.sqrt(d):s);const m=Math.max(...sc2);const e=sc2.map(s=>Math.exp(s-m));const Z=e.reduce((a,b)=>a+b,0);const p=e.map(x=>x/Z);const box=document.getElementById('bars');box.innerHTML='';p.forEach((w,j)=>{const r=document.createElement('div');r.className='bar';r.innerHTML='<span class=\"lab\">key '+(j+1)+' (score '+sc2[j].toFixed(1)+')</span><div class=\"track\"><div class=\"fill\" style=\"width:'+(w*100).toFixed(1)+'%\"></div></div><span class=\"num\">'+w.toFixed(3)+'</span>';box.appendChild(r);});const g=p.reduce((a,x)=>a+x*(1-x),0);document.getElementById('stats').textContent='Scores fed to softmax range from '+Math.min(...sc2).toFixed(1)+' to '+m.toFixed(1)+'. Largest weight: '+Math.max(...p).toFixed(3)+'. Gradient signal Σp(1−p): '+g.toFixed(4)+' (maximum possible here ≈ 0.833).';}sl.addEventListener('input',render);sc.addEventListener('click',()=>{scaled=!scaled;sc.setAttribute('aria-pressed',scaled?'true':'false');sc.textContent='Scaling by 1/√d_k: '+(scaled?'on':'off');render();});document.getElementById('rn').addEventListener('click',()=>{seed=Math.floor(Math.random()*1e9);gen();render();});gen();render();</script>"
}
